+# Part 2 local result
+
+Local tooling only. No network, account, console or debugger contact; no upload, original-mod/config/runtime edit, shared checkpoint write or commit. One opt-in Lua runner, one JSONL/TSV comparator and focused local tests are prepared in this folder. Neither tool has been installed or run in a game.
+
+Current engine evidence remains **0/17 API surfaces console-proven**, **13 implemented-untested + 4 with known full-API differences**, and **0/33 reflected methods console-proven**. The l16 test stopped before the FName constructor because the fresh prefix copyin returned EFAULT. Startup admission, symbol presence, host fixtures and this tooling do not fill that gap. Same-game PC reference remains pending because the user owns PS5 only.
+
+The two saved release/console files rehash identically: `Scripts/main.lua` SHA-256 `f586043a1ca5708113e8ee31532d6396cbb0866daeae473722dd8880b6559658`; empty `enabled.txt` SHA-256 `e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855`. No extra release files were added. Saved archive identity is `a9f7ed004dd053e02f6206d8ed6886174f9b5aaecf55244447a2c5fb9d6fa7fb` (not freshly downloaded). UEHelpers saved source SHA-256 is `5a8f6609e555eee4a535f51d21fcdef768ac654bf4d4abe283c719b1c12215a7`. All five binding source hashes match the actual l16 receipt; exact paths/digests are in `PROVENANCE.json`.
+
+| Release flow / API | Current status | Tool coverage / remaining evidence |
+|---|---|---|
+| Chunk: RegisterKeyBind | implemented-untested | Six original key codes/order; acceptance and independently guarded actual delivery are separate |
+| Chunk: RegisterLoadMapPreHook | behaves differently | Optional registration may succeed while deferred arm permanently refuses; real map event still pending |
+| Chunk: print | implemented-untested | Tag/string/newline and return count; independent exact output capture required |
+| F7: ExecuteInGameThread | behaves differently | Prospero marshal carrier differs from PC queues; accepted/queued callback is not actual native game-thread delivery |
+| F7 scan: FindFirstOf | implemented-untested | Live ItemDatabaseSubsystem must match the controlled fixture |
+| UObject:IsValid | implemented-untested | Live and invalid-wrapper semantics; target lifetime remains unproved |
+| UObject.__index / __newindex | implemented-untested | Representative Pawn read, ShadowOffset assignment and nested Font.Size write/readback/revert; method/property layouts remain unproved |
+| FName/FText/FString:ToString | implemented-untested | Real native fixtures plus constructor roundtrips; ordinary Lua strings are not conversion proof |
+| Controller lookup: require | behaves differently | UEHelpers export/cache; native preload/retained-buffer searchers replace disk/C routes; inventory alone remains observation-only |
+| UEHelpers init: CreateInvalidObject | implemented-untested | Two import cache initializers and invalid-controller fallback require actual wrappers |
+| UEHelpers: FindAllOf | implemented-untested | Enumeration and falsy-only fallback; an empty table does not trigger Controller fallback |
+| UMG: StaticFindObject | implemented-untested | Original class/default-object paths; local traversal rather than verified native finder |
+| UMG: FName | behaves differently | Release uses default Add1; Find0/Unicode/Replace2 extension cases; native Replace2 refusal preserved as an observation |
+| UMG: StaticConstructObject | implemented-untested | Original class/outer/FName arguments; explicit owned fixtures and verified cleanup |
+| UScriptStruct / array / OUT marshalling | implemented-untested | Nested Font.Size, ShadowOffset, controller arrays and original 12-argument trace with projected HitResult point/normal; all other layout/ownership behavior remains pending |
+| UMG: FText | implemented-untested | Native text constructor and roundtrip; real SetText ownership/copying remains pending |
+| Later asset fallback: LoadAsset | implemented-untested | Invalid lookup → load → second lookup, preserving three returns; explicit asset/reset context required |
+
+The release defines functions at chunk load but calls only six RegisterKeyBind registrations, optional RegisterLoadMapPreHook and the Loaded print there. F7 dispatches `toggleMenu`; `showMenu(true)` scans the database before `buildUI`. Scan conversion comes before UEHelpers/controller/UMG lookup. UEHelpers import initializes two invalid caches; its controller search falls back only on a falsy collection. Root `Create` precedes conditional StaticConstructObject fallback. UMG tree construction evaluates class lookup and FName before StaticConstructObject. Native nested font/vector writes can silently fail under the release's pcall paths, so readback/restore is explicit in the probe.
+
+Enter first resolves controller/pawn fallbacks, reads location/rotation, and performs the 12-argument ground trace. It then looks up the cooked pickup class; only an invalid class triggers LoadAsset and another lookup. BeginDeferredActorSpawnFromClass/FinishSpawningActor precede pickup validation, ItemId comparison, quantity/auto-destroy writes and enabled/visibility/collision changes; failure conditionally destroys the actor. Map cleanup occurs independently on a transition. The runner does not implement or autoexecute this actor-spawn chain. All 33 actual reflected names remain listed as untested in the manifest; the original mod must still visibly open/close/reopen its own readable UMG menu, lock/unlock input safely and spawn a real valid pickup before the broader ladder can advance.
+
+The strict comparator rejects missing, extra, duplicate or out-of-order cases and unknown parity. Presence is emitted as binding inventory with `behavior_proved=false`. Local doubles produce only `fixture-pass`; missing context/permissions/witnesses produce `skipped`, absent bindings `unavailable`, incorrect native results/readbacks/cleanup `failed`. Registration alone can prove its narrow acceptance case but cannot satisfy the separately required delivery case. Loader searcher inventory and Replace2 observations intentionally remain unproved, so a full-suite match is currently impossible. No skipped or matching failed record becomes parity.
+
+Final local verification and tool hashes are saved in `LOCAL-RECEIPT.json` and `tests.log`. These are local tool-validation receipts, not engine captures. The available standalone Lua is 5.5.1, while target Lua 5.4 execution is pending. Testing the runner with Lua objects does not prove ABI, native userdata layout, callback delivery, engine-thread identity or cleanup in Townfall.
+
+Off-by-default runtime tooling remains planned-only: crash reporting that chains the previous handler needs independently reviewed handler ownership, safe crash-context capture and bounded log lifetime; a LAN Lua console needs a real guarded Lua owner/lifetime, authenticated disabled-by-default transport and serialized dispatch through a proved carrier; a read-only debugger needs verified object/memory lifetimes, read boundaries and thread scheduling. This folder implements none of these runtime interfaces. It supplies no sandbox/credential workaround or external service connection.
+
+Preserve the authorized order: resolve the live constructor-prefix refusal and obtain native constructor/roundtrip evidence → off-by-default runtime tooling → runtime/config controller-to-original-key translation → the original mod's UMG menu → actual pickup spawn → conformance and more immutable downloaded mods → deferred B/C/A capabilities (#1/#3/#6, then #4, then #5/#2/#7/#8). Those deferred capabilities retain their three console passes across reboots, saved logs and separate user approval requirements. This local work authorizes no future console action.
+
+Future PC reference plan: obtain an explicitly authorized same-game PC run from an available PC owner; no such machine or run is present here. Pin each platform's executable/runtime hashes separately, matching game content build, exact mod/helper/runner hashes and a controlled comparable scene/save/scenario/context. Independently establish the native thread witness and owned object fixtures, collect raw logs and cleanup receipts, then record all manifest cases in order. Preserve unavailable/skipped/errors rather than manufacturing reference values. Run the local comparator on the independently harvested PC and PS5 records. Another title, mock object table, manually edited attestation or PC-shaped host output cannot establish Townfall parity.
